WEBVTT

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:08.210
Grandmaster Den!

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:09.530
Grandmaster Eizan!

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:10.680
It's an emergency!

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:12.460
What's wrong, Hane-chan?

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:15.700
The Tenshifu is being attacked by Zensei!

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:19.080
Those fiends! What are they after?

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.780
That's not all!

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:23.350
The Tenshi got caught up in the fighting!

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:24.580
What?

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:26.420
There's too many of them...

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:28.950
At this rate, everyone will die!

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:30.820
Go, Eizan.

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:33.700
Save your brothers.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.960
But protecting you is...

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:37.840
That's an order!

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:39.720
Understood.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:43.900
Hane-chan, Kei-chan. 
Look after Shinchuu-sama.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.730
You can count on us, Master.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.950
They can beat Zensei, right?

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.580
The Tenshifu won't be destroyed, will it?

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:57.330
Hane, you...

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:00.760
Let me introduce myself.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.610
I'm the acting Master of Zensei...

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:06.310
Kyoukei.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:44.760
<b>23:                Repose</b>

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:47.030
Let me introduce myself.

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:50.970
I'm the acting Master of Zensei, Kyoukei.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:03:01.610
<b><i>Hitorinoshita -The Outcast</i> comic is now being published in Shonen JUMP+!</b>

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:54.180
What? You are?

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:57.310
Is it really that surprising?

00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:01.280
Aren't you very familiar with Zensei?

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:07.080
I'd think you could easily 
imagine Zensei members

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:10.460
infiltrating Ryuukosan 
and posing as disciples.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:14.420
What do you want?

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:18.690
I approached you for one reason:

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:21.850
I want to know about the Koushin War.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:29.660
To do that, I had to investigate Chou 
Kaigi, the central figure in the war.

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:36.230
The other Zensei members searched for him

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:40.060
and finally discovered his whereabouts.

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:43.740
However, he was already dead.

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:52.270
I decided to infiltrate Ryuukosan, 
where Chou Kaigi trained.

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:59.680
But you'd never tell me about the 
Koushin War if I asked about it.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:02.970
I had nearly given up.

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:09.200
However, by sheer coincidence, I found a clue.

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:14.300
I've been waiting for an 
opportunity to use that clue.

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:19.730
An opportunity to speak with 
you alone, face to face,

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:22.320
just like we are now.

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:26.030
What do you want to know?

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:29.840
When Chou Kaigi left Ryuukosan,

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:34.480
you and Chou Jiiei, the current Tenshi,

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:39.010
took different routes down the 
mountain to bring back Chou Kaigi.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:44.080
However, unable to find Kaigi,

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:48.960
you were attacked and ended 
up in your current state.

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:50.430
Isn't that right?

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:54.620
How do you know that?

00:04:54.620 --> 00:05:01.350
It's true that only you, the Tenshi, 
and a handful of others know about this.

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:06.050
But it's obvious enough 
if you think about it.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:09.760
I heard a rumor that you and the Tenshi

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:14.110
went after a problem child 
who left the Tenshifu.

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:19.370
It goes without saying that that 
problem child was Chou Kaigi.

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:25.250
And it's clear your scars 
are the result of torture.

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:30.350
So what did your torturers 
want to know so badly

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:33.790
that they were willing to 
torture you so much?

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:37.190
Most likely, it was Chou Kaigi's whereabouts.

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:40.770
My inference is correct, isn't it?

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:47.300
By the way, this sneak attack 
against Ryuukosan was set in motion

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:50.250
based on my inference alone.

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:54.210
If I'm wrong, the others will kill me.

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:58.950
I had no idea you were this smart.

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:03.650
But I can't say you're right.

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:09.130
The Tenshi and I did split up 
and descend the mountain

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:14.090
in order to find Kaigi, 
and only I was attacked.

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:20.200
They tortured me so I'd 
reveal Kaigi's whereabouts.

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:25.600
But I had no way of knowing where he'd gone.

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:31.480
I still regret that I couldn't find him!

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:38.280
You truly are tight-lipped.

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:40.840
Come in.

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:00.840
He's Ro Ryou, a Meikon user.

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:05.770
He can manipulate your soul 
and extract your memories.

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:09.870
Still won't tell me the truth?

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:14.060
Or do you want to hear more 
about what I've inferred?

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:17.070
Very well.

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:23.010
I looked after you for the three 
years I was at Ryuukosan.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:26.630
One day, I saw you

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:31.110
desperately trying to stay awake.

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:44.330
Grandmaster, is it true that 
Grandmaster Den never sleeps?

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:47.970
Is he okay without sleeping?

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:56.230
Someone as strong-willed as 
Shinchuu doesn't need to sleep.

00:07:56.230 --> 00:07:59.520
That's amazing. How long has he not slept?

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:03.440
For a long time now.

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:09.470
I believe it's been since he 
came to look like he does now.

00:08:10.470 --> 00:08:11.890
Wow...

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:16.250
I was so excited to learn this.

00:08:16.250 --> 00:08:21.150
After all, it presented me 
with a certain possibility.

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:24.490
It's not that you don't need to sleep.

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:29.040
You <i>can't</i> sleep. You're afraid to sleep.

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:34.170
You descended the mountain 
to search for Chou Kaigi.

00:08:35.020 --> 00:08:40.470
The men who attacked you were 
searching for Chou Kaigi, as well.

00:08:41.490 --> 00:08:43.780
No matter how much they tortured you,

00:08:43.780 --> 00:08:47.630
they failed to get Chou Kaigi's 
whereabouts out of you.

00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:53.440
They assumed you failed to find Chou Kaigi.

00:08:54.730 --> 00:08:58.210
Otherwise, they wouldn't have let you live.

00:08:58.520 --> 00:09:00.170
Isn't that right?

00:09:00.170 --> 00:09:04.690
If someone at Ryuukosan knew 
of Chou Kaigi's whereabouts,

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:07.570
they'd only get in their way.

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:13.730
And since that day, you 
haven't been able to sleep.

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:17.100
It's as though you're afraid of something.

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:21.170
Why are you so afraid of sleeping?

00:09:21.510 --> 00:09:23.850
Then it came to me.

00:09:24.260 --> 00:09:28.930
Sleeping deprives people 
of their self-control.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:34.380
Yes. What you're afraid of 
is talking in your sleep.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:41.070
Since the day you descended the mountain 
to search for Chou Kaigi and were tortured,

00:09:41.070 --> 00:09:44.270
you've kept a secret that
must never be revealed.

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:47.850
You met Chou Kaigi.

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:54.210
You had a conversation that you had to 
hide from your master and the Tenshi,

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:55.800
even if it meant lying to them.

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:01.340
Well? Was my inference mistaken?

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:06.260
You've thought long and 
hard about this, boy.

00:10:06.860 --> 00:10:09.240
But you're wrong.

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:11.960
I didn't meet Kaigi.

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:17.760
You can cut off my limbs and 
crush my meridian system,

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:21.590
but I never found him!

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:26.470
No matter who's asking, 
that's my only answer.

00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:33.080
Grandmaster Den, I know 
how tight-lipped you are.

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:35.770
That's why I brought him.

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:37.300
Do it.

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:42.330
Don't.

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:43.620
Don't do this!

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:45.360
I don't know anything!

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:51.960
The Tenshifu could return at any time.

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:54.870
Find his memory of that time quickly.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:57.840
Once you've got it,

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:02.050
don't forget to erase his memories 
of the incident and today.

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:03.920
I can't.

00:11:04.570 --> 00:11:09.620
His soul is stronger than 
anything I've ever seen.

00:11:10.070 --> 00:11:12.780
Just entering his soul is hard enough.

00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:17.850
I'm not sure I could find a particular 
memory even if I had a few months.

00:11:18.890 --> 00:11:22.480
It's impossible to find it in 
such a short amount of time.

00:11:23.210 --> 00:11:24.860
You keep watch.

00:11:24.860 --> 00:11:28.860
I'll copy as many of his memories 
as I can in the meantime.

00:11:58.340 --> 00:12:00.270
I did it.

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:03.630
I copied all his memories.

00:12:04.420 --> 00:12:06.230
We have no further business here.

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:08.490
We should go.

00:12:09.050 --> 00:12:11.160
Wait, Hane.

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:14.730
Just leave him.

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:17.710
It's over now. Let's go.

00:12:20.890 --> 00:12:23.540
Come on, hurry up before someone comes.

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:26.030
If you want to die, have it your way!

00:12:26.030 --> 00:12:27.600
I'm going!

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:30.210
Damn.

00:12:39.030 --> 00:12:40.350
Hane...

00:12:41.310 --> 00:12:43.200
Not bad.

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:47.680
I can't believe you've been planning 
this for the past three years.

00:12:48.310 --> 00:12:53.860
It seems everything turned 
out just as you planned it.

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:58.870
There's nothing I can do to stop you now.

00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:00.610
Yes.

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:05.380
Are you going to leave me like this and go?

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:06.980
Yes.

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:13.780
Zensei, my ass.

00:13:13.780 --> 00:13:18.270
You arrogantly proclaim that 
you're defending your interests,

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:22.050
but all you're doing is 
selfishly rampaging about.

00:13:22.050 --> 00:13:25.980
You're nothing more than 
a group of scoundrels.

00:13:26.510 --> 00:13:30.720
You destroy everything while taking 
responsibility for nothing.

00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:33.530
You're losers!

00:13:34.760 --> 00:13:37.600
Please stop, Grandmaster Den.

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:38.800
This isn't like you.

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:42.040
Don't casually call me "master"!

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:44.920
You don't have the right, you trash!

00:13:51.070 --> 00:13:53.110
That's enough. I understand.

00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:58.330
I will do the responsible thing 
and take your life.

00:14:01.030 --> 00:14:03.820
You can't handle it.

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:05.800
I'm one of the Ten Elders.

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:10.990
You could never kill someone of my station!

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:15.120
Please don't provoke me any further.

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:38.000
<i>Finally...</i>

00:14:38.630 --> 00:14:40.450
<i>Is that really your decision?</i>

00:14:43.700 --> 00:14:47.430
Are you that determined to know, Shinchuu?

00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:54.030
I won't give up until I hear you say it.

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:05.040
Do you understand now? 
That's what we're doing.

00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:08.360
Do you still want to take me back?

00:15:09.960 --> 00:15:12.960
No. You can't return to the Tenshifu.

00:15:13.320 --> 00:15:15.020
You mustn't meet with our master, either.

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:21.110
But if what you said is true, 
how are you still alive?

00:15:22.090 --> 00:15:25.070
I'm the fourth brother who swore a vow.

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:28.480
Having surpassed the power of Mukonsei, 
I've come to understand something.

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:30.580
Understand?

00:15:31.020 --> 00:15:32.080
Understand what?

00:15:34.940 --> 00:15:38.480
The innermost secrets of the kitaigen style.

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:41.300
The kitaigen style?

00:15:41.680 --> 00:15:43.680
Hey, Kaigi-san!

00:15:44.660 --> 00:15:46.240
Let's go!

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:49.820
Shinchuu, come with me.

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:52.640
You can't return to Ryuukosan now.

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:57.820
I can't. My master and the others 
are waiting for me to return.

00:15:58.800 --> 00:16:02.370
You'll have to keep this 
secret until you die.

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:05.290
You can't even tell your master.

00:16:05.950 --> 00:16:07.440
Are you prepared to do that?

00:16:08.370 --> 00:16:11.070
I can't get them involved.

00:16:13.260 --> 00:16:17.550
If I'd known this was the answer, 
I never would have asked.

00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:19.940
I told you because you're you, Shinchuu.

00:16:21.220 --> 00:16:24.910
I'd rather die than tell anyone else.

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:28.340
Shinchuu, the rest is up to you.

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:29.840
Farewell.

00:16:33.160 --> 00:16:34.220
Shinchuu!

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:36.420
Wake up!

00:16:36.420 --> 00:16:37.710
Shinchuu!

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:38.960
Do you recognize us?

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:41.540
Master...

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:44.890
Jiiei-senpai...

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:52.860
I couldn't find Kaigi.

00:16:53.460 --> 00:16:58.060
But they still questioned 
me about his whereabouts.

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:01.100
I'm sorry.

00:17:01.570 --> 00:17:06.970
Not only did I fail to bring Kaigi back, 
but I returned in this condition.

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:10.010
That's enough. Don't speak, Shinchuu.

00:17:10.610 --> 00:17:16.300
I promise I'll identify the 
ones who attacked you.

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:18.960
I will avenge you.

00:17:20.050 --> 00:17:24.030
Master, I'm sorry.

00:17:29.340 --> 00:17:30.680
What's going on?

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:40.030
Shinchuu!

00:17:41.400 --> 00:17:42.820
What are you doing?

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:46.200
Master, please.

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:48.930
Please let me die.

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:53.000
I'll only burden you by living.

00:17:54.020 --> 00:17:56.000
Please!

00:17:56.000 --> 00:17:57.380
You fool!

00:17:57.380 --> 00:18:00.320
What have you learned here?!

00:18:04.280 --> 00:18:05.340
Listen to me.

00:18:05.860 --> 00:18:10.860
You're like me: a man seeking enlightenment.

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:16.600
You must respect life and overcome 
whatever obstacles come your way.

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:20.860
You can't end your own life!

00:18:22.350 --> 00:18:25.810
No matter how hard it is, 
you must endure it and live on.

00:18:25.810 --> 00:18:27.840
And remember this:

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:33.720
anytime you're ready to give 
everything up, you must train.

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:37.820
Master, I understand.

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:43.340
Now swear to me you will.

00:18:43.340 --> 00:18:44.280
Yes, Master.

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:52.340
Shinchuu, breakfast.

00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:57.570
I'm sorry for troubling you, Jiiei-senpai.

00:18:58.690 --> 00:19:01.150
Don't be that way, Shinchuu.

00:19:01.150 --> 00:19:04.280
You were injured while 
working for the Tenshifu.

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:09.270
You have nothing to feel sorry for.

00:19:10.130 --> 00:19:14.990
Besides, I can skip boring training 
sessions if I'm looking after you.

00:19:15.470 --> 00:19:17.580
As far as I'm concerned, you're helping me.

00:19:18.230 --> 00:19:21.380
I don't feel sorry.

00:19:21.380 --> 00:19:22.580
So you say,

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:28.300
but you kept apologizing to me 
and our master in your sleep.

00:19:52.480 --> 00:19:55.450
Now is the time to train.

00:19:56.280 --> 00:19:59.250
Now is the time to train.

00:20:00.100 --> 00:20:05.050
<i>I'm sorry, Kaigi. I shouldn't have asked.</i>

00:20:05.580 --> 00:20:08.350
<i>I shouldn't have returned to Ryuukosan.</i>

00:20:09.530 --> 00:20:12.560
<i>I did this to myself.</i>

00:20:13.300 --> 00:20:15.720
<i>I'm sorry, Master.</i>

00:20:16.910 --> 00:20:19.890
<i>I've been blocked in on all sides.</i>

00:20:19.890 --> 00:20:22.450
<i>I don't know where to go.</i>

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:26.420
<i>Everyone at Ryuukosan, I'm sorry.</i>

00:20:26.820 --> 00:20:29.610
<i>I'm sorry you have to look after me.</i>

00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:32.530
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:20:33.300 --> 00:20:35.860
<i>I'm sorry, everyone.</i>

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:45.330
<i>When I learned what Kaigi was doing, 
I should've made up my mind.</i>

00:20:46.940 --> 00:20:50.180
<i>I should've ended my life, though it meant</i>

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:53.150
<i>violating the vow I swore to my master.</i>

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:55.610
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:21:03.600 --> 00:21:05.400
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:21:06.150 --> 00:21:09.970
<i>I should've died back then.</i>

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:14.330
Grandmaster Den...

00:21:16.220 --> 00:21:17.610
Sleep well.

00:23:25.960 --> 00:23:27.210
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:27.210 --> 00:23:29.800
Goodbye, Grandmaster Den.

00:23:30.210 --> 00:23:32.600
Rest in peace.

00:23:33.970 --> 00:23:38.030
Next time on the final episode of
<i>Hitorinoshita - The Outcast</i>, "Beijing."

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>24:                      Beijing</b>

00:23:38.030 --> 00:23:39.210
Don't miss it.
